Experiment Summary - Multi-Scale Genomic Feature Extraction
============================================================

Date: January 14, 2026

Objective:
Implement a multi-scale feature extraction mechanism that processes genomic data at different 
resolutions (promoter regions, gene bodies, enhancer regions) and fuses these features using 
a genomic context attention mechanism to improve cell type annotation accuracy and F1 scores.

Implementation Status: COMPLETED

Key Components Developed:
1. Multi-Scale Feature Extractor - Processes genomic data at different resolutions using 
   specialized convolutional layers with varying kernel sizes (3, 7, 15, 31)
2. Genomic Context Attention - Weighs features based on known regulatory element annotations
3. Enhanced Model Architecture - Integrates multi-scale processing with genomic attention

Technical Approach:
- Separated processing of local regulatory elements (promoters) and distal elements (enhancers)
- Applied genomic context attention to emphasize biologically relevant interactions
- Used hierarchical feature fusion to combine multi-scale information
- Maintained compatibility with existing pipeline architecture

Validation Results:
- All architectural components tested and validated successfully
- Input/output dimensions verified for correctness
- Component integration confirmed working properly

Expected Improvements:
- Enhanced cell type classification accuracy through multi-scale genomic features
- Improved F1 scores via genomic context-aware attention mechanisms
- Better generalization across different cell types due to biologically-informed architecture

Files Created:
- src/models/genomic_multi_scale_attention.py (core implementation)
- src/cell_type_annotation_multiscale.py (enhanced model)
- test_architecture.py (validation script)
- IMPLEMENTATION_SUMMARY.md (technical documentation)

The implementation is complete and ready for training with genomic data to demonstrate 
quantitative improvements in cell type annotation metrics.